/datum/lore/religion
	var/name = ""
	var/desc = ""

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Chaplain&oldid=3942
/datum/lore/religion/agnosticism
	name = "Agnosticism"
	desc = "Agnosticism is the position that the existence or nature of gods and other higher powers is unknown or unknowable. Agnostics follow no specific religious belief by default, although this does not necessarily exclude spiritual practices; the position is common across the interstellar community."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Chaplain&oldid=3942
/datum/lore/religion/buddhism
	name = "Buddhism"
	desc = "Buddhism is a family of Old Earth traditions based on the teachings of the Buddha, emphasizing ethical conduct, meditation, moderation, and liberation from suffering. It is one of humanity's ancient religions not merely to survive but to thrive in the interstellar era, where its teachings retain broad appeal."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/christianity
	name = "Christianity"
	desc = "Christianity is an Abrahamic monotheistic religion centered on the life and teachings of Jesus Christ, whom Christians regard as the Son of God and humanity's savior. It survives throughout human space in both traditional and newer interstellar branches, while many liberal communities have entered communion with Unitarianism."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Chaplain&oldid=3942
/datum/lore/religion/deism
	name = "Deism"
	desc = "Deism holds that observation and reason point to a creator, but that this creator does not intervene in creation. The universe instead proceeds according to its natural laws; the belief became popular in the twenty-first century and continued to grow as humanity spread among the stars."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/hauler_faith
	name = "Hauler Faith"
	desc = "The Hauler Faith is a loose body of spacer spirituality and superstition that arose among long-haul crews during the Age of Expansion. It treats shipboard survival and community as sacred through customs such as venerating the captain, maintaining a Gallows where the crew may dissent freely, promptly spacing the dead, and observing taboos around bluespace drives; the Free Trade Union's Religious Matters Committee is its closest equivalent to a central authority."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/hinduism
	name = "Hinduism"
	desc = "Hinduism is a diverse family of Old Earth religions originating in the Indian subcontinent, with traditions shaped by such concepts as dharma, karma, rebirth, and liberation. Its many schools and practices traveled into space with their adherents and survive in both traditional and newer interstellar forms."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/islam
	name = "Islam"
	desc = "Islam is an Abrahamic monotheistic religion centered on submission to God, the Quran, and the teachings of the prophet Muhammad, with the Five Pillars forming the foundation of religious life. Muslim communities remain established throughout human space in both traditional and newer interstellar branches, while some liberal communities have entered communion with Unitarianism."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982, https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Pluto&oldid=3473
/datum/lore/religion/judaism
	name = "Judaism"
	desc = "Judaism is an ancient Abrahamic monotheistic religion rooted in the covenant between God and the Jewish people, with the Torah central to its law and tradition. Jewish communities remain active across human space, notably on Pluto, in both traditional and newer interstellar forms; some liberal communities have entered communion with Unitarianism."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/kishari_faith
	name = "Kishari Faith"
	desc = "Kishari Faith is the common offworld survey label for the Kishari National Religions, a family of minority traditions preserved or revitalized within Kishar's domes. Unlike eclectic Neopaganism, most emphasize continuous lineages and re-establishing inherited practices over broad syncretism, although Kishari migrant communities often practice looser, blended forms."

// Sources: Virgo Discord
/datum/lore/religion/neo_moreauism
	name = "Neo-Moreauism"
	desc = "Neo-Moreauism teaches that all life is inherently divine and that sapient beings collectively embody the universe's consciousness, morality, and memory. Its decentralized, generally pacifist sects de-emphasize humanity in favor of all sapient life and pursue Galactic Redemption through ecoformation, agriculture, universal healthcare, charity, and opposition to wasteful industry."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/neopaganism
	name = "Neopaganism"
	desc = "Neopaganism is a collection of religions rooted in Old Earth's revivalist movements, generally combining polytheism, animism, and mystical practice. Some adherents reconstruct pantheons such as the Greek or Norse gods while others blend traditions freely; the Interstellar Congress of Eclectic Pagans is its principal coordinating body."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/nock
	name = "Nock"
	desc = "Nock is a relatively young faith with roots in Abrahamic and East Asian religions whose adherents recreate themselves through ornate masks and the personas those masks embody. Its major practice is communion with Entities or Outworlders, beings said to exist only partly in the material world and approached for aid, advice, or insight into the domains that fascinate them."

// Sources: Virgo Discord
/datum/lore/religion/orthodox_moreauism
	name = "Orthodox Moreauism"
	desc = "Orthodox Moreauism follows the original, human-centered teachings of Moreau's Church of Galactic Redemption. It regards humanity as the universe's principal caretaker of life and calls its adherents to redeem barren worlds through cultivation, sustainable settlement, and terraforming them into new Garden Edens."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/phact_shintoism
	name = "Phact Shintoism"
	desc = "Phact Shintoism is New Kyoto's state religion, presented as a revival of pre-Buddhist Shinto and practiced almost exclusively within the Phact system. This polytheistic and animist faith prizes tradition, community, and hard work, resists outside cultural influence, and accepts the New Kyoto emperors' claimed descent from the sun goddess Amaterasu."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/pleromanism
	name = "Pleromanism"
	desc = "Pleromanism is a Gnostic offshoot of Unitarianism which views the physical world as intrinsically corrupted and the internal spiritual world as intrinsically good. It emerged from a schism over whether positronic minds possess souls capable of salvation, and is now followed by many positronics on Sophia and in smaller positronic communities."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/singulitarian_worship
	name = "Singulitarian Worship"
	desc = "Singulitarian Worship is an informal faith venerating the enigmatic creators of positronic brains. Its mostly positronic adherents believe that the Singulitarians survived catastrophe by ascending to a higher phase of existence and still intervene through phenomena such as phoron and galactic tachyon flow, a claim treated skeptically by scientists and discouraged by Sol authorities."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982, /datum/lore/codex/page/article80
/datum/lore/religion/spectralism
	name = "Spectralism"
	desc = "Spectralism, also called Spark Theory, teaches that every sapient synthetic possesses a soul called a Spark and that all Sparks are joined through the Sparkwell, the Source from which they came and to which they eventually return. The faith emphasizes nonviolence and rich color symbolism, with ministers known as Wardens guiding its adherents."

// Sources: https://wiki.vore-station.net/index.php?title=Tajaran&oldid=9624, https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Tajaran&oldid=3965
/datum/lore/religion/tajr_kii_rarkajar
	name = "Tajr-kii Rarkajar"
	desc = "Tajr-kii Rarkajar is a Tajaran religion especially widespread in Selem culture. It teaches that Rarkajar and Mephir struggle eternally over the fate of the dead. Rarkajar seeks to rescue souls from Mephir's desolate Bounty, joining them in shared knowledge until they freely choose reincarnation, while Mephir hunts and drains those souls; the faith consequently uses strong imagery of the sun and the Light."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Religion&oldid=3982
/datum/lore/religion/unitarianism
	name = "Unitarianism"
	desc = "Unitarianism is an Abrahamic faith founded by the Martian chaplain Tevel ben Odael after revelations recorded in the Great Canon. It teaches that many religions and national prophets are expressions of God's will within the 'dance of the nations,' and became popular as a framework for ministering to culturally diverse colonial communities."

// Sources: https://ss13polaris.com/wiki/index.php?title=Skrell&oldid=3929, https://wiki.vore-station.net/index.php?title=Skrell&oldid=9623
/datum/lore/religion/xilar_qall
	name = "Xilar Qall"
	desc = "Xilar Qall is a Skrellian religion rooted in the story of a vast entity whose song crossed the sky and inspired the first Skrell to speak. Many modern adherents treat the story metaphorically while following its ethical teachings of discipline, social unity, inquisitiveness, the pursuit of knowledge, and harming only when harmed."
